{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"rg --files -g AGENTS.md -g '*commit-graph*' -g '*backend-go*'; cat .pose/specs/2026-11-16-pose-doctor-recommends-the-commit-graph.md; nl -ba pose-mcp/internal/cli/doctor_commit_graph.go; nl -ba pose-mcp/internal/cli/doctor_commit_graph_test.go\"","aggregated_output":"locales/pt-BR/AGENTS.md\nAGENTS.md\npose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/AGENTS.md\npose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/locales/pt-BR/AGENTS.md\n---\nslug: pose-doctor-recommends-the-commit-graph\nstatus: in-progress\ncreated_at: 2026-11-16\ncompleted_at:        # stamped on the transition to status: done\nsupersedes:          # slug of the superseded spec (when applicable)\ndepends_on:          # prerequisites, inline list: other-spec, milestone:<roadmap>/<id>, roadmap:<slug>\nremediates:          # optional explicit links: spec:slug@defect-fix, finding:rva-<16hex>/F1@revert (never inferred from depends_on)\npriority:            # integer >= 0 (lower = higher priority); ordering preference, not a blocker\ncomponents: pose-mcp\ntask_type: feature\nsurface:             # optional: minimal | standard | full (default) — minimal drops Tasks and derivable report sections; `pose specs facts <slug>` derives them\ndelivers: capability:doctor-recommends-the-commit-graph\n---\n\n# Spec: pose-doctor-recommends-the-commit-graph\n\n## 1. Intent\n\n### Goal\nFazer o `pose doctor` recomendar, e o `pose doctor --fix` escrever, o commit-graph do Git com filtros de Bloom de caminhos alterados num projeto cujo histórico é grande o bastante para pesar, e fazer o CI do pose-dist escrevê-lo antes dos gates.\n\n### Business value\nA spec `pose-review-ledger-is-read-once-per-operation` mediu, na primeira chamada `pose_closeout_state` de um servidor MCP no harne8, 1.116 comandos `git log -1 --format=%H -- <path>` somando 81 s: cada um percorre o histórico do pose-dist (3.528 commits) até achar o último commit que tocou o arquivo. Com o commit-graph com caminhos alterados (`git commit-graph write --reachable --changed-paths`), cada consulta cai de 47 ms para 2 ms, sem mudar a saída do Git, e a primeira chamada cai de 136 s para 59 s. É manutenção do repositório, que o motor não faz sozinho numa leitura de governança; o `doctor` é o lugar onde o POSE já recomenda e aplica remediações seguras.\n\n### Constraints\n- A verificação só lê arquivos do Git; não roda nada que escreva.\n- A correção só escreve sob o diretório de objetos do Git, é idempotente e reversível (apagar o arquivo devolve o estado anterior), como as demais do registro do `doctor --fix`.\n- Uma instalação nova, com histórico pequeno, continua sem passos pendentes.\n\n### Non-goals\n- Escrever o commit-graph durante uma operação de governança.\n- Manter o commit-graph atualizado a cada commit (o `git gc` e o `git maintenance` já o reescrevem preservando os filtros).\n\n---\n\n## 2. Requirements\n\n### Functional\n- R1: When the project root is a Git repository whose HEAD has at least 500 commits, and Git's own trace of a last-commit lookup by path shows no changed-path Bloom filter consulted, `pose doctor` shall report the check `git.commit-graph` at level `next`, with the command that writes it; the judgement follows whichever commit-graph Git loads (its own object directory or an alternate, a single file or a chain).\n- R2: `pose doctor --fix --yes` shall remediate `git.commit-graph` by running `git commit-graph write --reachable --changed-paths --max-new-filters=-1` in the project root, so `commitGraph.maxNewFilters` cannot leave commits without filters, after which the check shall report `ok`.\n- R3: A repository with fewer than 500 commits on HEAD, or one whose last-commit lookup Git answers from the filters, shall report `ok`; a project root that is not a Git repository, has no commit on HEAD, has a shallow history or has no file in HEAD's tree shall not report the check; Git warnings printed by a successful lookup, such as an unreadable commit-graph, shall report `warn`; no diagnostic command shall fetch from a remote; any other failure to read the state shall report `warn` with a bounded description of the failure; when Git configuration keeps it from reading commit-graphs or their changed-path filters, `pose doctor` shall report `git.commit-graph-reads` at `warn`, naming the setting, instead of recommending a rewrite.\n- R4: The pose-dist CI jobs that check out the full history shall write the commit-graph with changed paths before their gates.\n\n### Non-functional\n- A verificação roda três comandos Git de leitura e uma busca do último commit de um arquivo com o trace2 ligado.\n\n### Security\n- A correção roda o Git com argumentos fixos no root do projeto; nenhuma entrada do usuário entra no comando.\n\n### Compatibility\n- Saída do `doctor` ganha um check novo; o formato do relatório não muda.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Technical Plan\n\n### Affected areas\n- `cli/doctor.go`: o check `git.commit-graph` e a entrada no registro de correções.\n- `cli/doctor_commit_graph.go`: a contagem do histórico e a pergunta ao Git, pelo trace2, se ele usa os filtros.\n- `.github/workflows/ci.yml`: o passo que escreve o commit-graph.\n\n### Artifacts\n- created: pose-mcp/internal/cli/doctor_commit_graph.go\n- created: pose-mcp/internal/cli/doctor_commit_graph_test.go\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/doctor.go\n- modified: .github/workflows/ci.yml\n- modified: .pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json\n\n### Delivery targets\n\n- capability:doctor-recommends-the-commit-graph module:pose-mcp profile:composed-capability entrypoint:pose-mcp/cmd/pose/main.go\n\nComposto em produção pelo `pose doctor` e pelo `pose doctor --fix`. Check permanente `doctor-recommends-the-commit-graph-integration`, evidenceClass `integration`, required: `go test ./internal/cli -run 'TestDoctorRecommendsTheCommitGraph|TestDoctorCommitGraph' -count=1`.\n\n### API/contract changes\n- Nenhuma.\n\n### Data/storage changes\n- Nenhuma no `.pose/`; a correção escreve o commit-graph sob `.git/objects/info/`.\n\n### Technical risks\n- O evento `bloom` do trace2 é saída de diagnóstico do Git; uma versão que o renomeie faria o check recomendar a correção sempre. A correção é inofensiva, e o teste de integração com o Git real reprova se o evento sumir.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Tasks\n\n### Implementation\n- [x] Check e correção `git.commit-graph` no `doctor` (R1, R2, R3).\n- [x] Passo do CI (R4).\n\n### Validation\n- [x] Testes com repositórios reais acima e abaixo do limite, com e sem filtros, com prova de reprovação.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Decisions\n\n### Decision D1\n- Date: 2026-11-16\n- Context: o follow-up F1 da spec `pose-review-ledger-is-read-once-per-operation`; o maintainer pediu para escrever o commit-graph nos checkouts dele e seguir com o F1.\n- Options considered: (a) o motor escreve o commit-graph numa leitura de governança; (b) o `doctor` recomenda e o `doctor --fix` escreve; (c) só documentar.\n- Decision: (b), com o limite de 500 commits.\n- Basis: R1, R2, R3\n- Rationale: (a) faria uma leitura escrever no repositório, o que a read view trata como mudança de entrada; (c) não chega a quem não lê o manual; (b) usa o caminho de remediação segura que o POSE já tem. Abaixo de cerca de 500 commits a busca de histórico custa poucos milissegundos.\n- Consequences: um projeto grande vê um passo pendente até rodar a correção.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Validation\n\n### Strategy\nTestes do `doctor` com repositórios Git reais; medição já registrada na spec de origem.\n\n### Deterministic checks\n\n#### Test\n- Command: `go test ./internal/cli -count=1`\n- Scope: pose-mcp\n- Expected: verde\n\n### Execution log\n- Date: 2026-11-16\n- Environment: Linux, Go 1.26, Git 2.56.\n- Notes: o teste monta uma instalação real, cria histórico acima de um limite reduzido e confere o check sem commit-graph (`next`, corrigível), depois da correção (`ok`), com um commit-graph sem filtros (`next`) e com um commit-graph dividido em camadas com filtros (`ok`); abaixo do limite, `ok`. Reprova quando a leitura ignora os chunks BIDX/BDAT, quando ignora a cadeia de camadas e quando a correção não está registrada. O guarda `TestEngineStartsGitOnlyThroughTheRawReader` reprovou a primeira versão, que chamava o Git direto; ela passou a usar `RawHistoryGit`. No checkout do pose-dist do maintainer, com o commit-graph escrito, o check dá `ok`. O `pose doctor` no harne8 passa de 900 s com o binário instalado antes desta spec, e por isso não foi medido lá.\n\n### Results summary\n- Successes: o `doctor` recomenda e escreve o commit-graph; o CI o escreve antes dos gates.\n- Failures: nenhuma.\n- Warnings: o `pose doctor` no harne8 leva mais de 900 s, já antes desta spec (follow-up F1).\n\n### Requirement trace\n- R1 [satisfied] test:TestDoctorRecommendsTheCommitGraph test:TestDoctorCommitGraphProbesALiteralPath check:doctor-recommends-the-commit-graph-integration\n- R2 [satisfied] test:TestDoctorRecommendsTheCommitGraph test:TestDoctorCommitGraphFixIgnoresMaxNewFilters\n- R3 [satisfied] test:TestDoctorRecommendsTheCommitGraph test:TestDoctorCommitGraphReportsAnUnreadableHistory test:TestDoctorCommitGraphTellsUnbornFromBroken test:TestDoctorCommitGraphNamesDisabledReads test:TestDoctorCommitGraphSkipsAShallowClone test:TestDoctorCommitGraphSkipsAnEmptyTree test:TestDoctorCommitGraphFollowsConfigurationPrecedence test:TestDoctorCommitGraphNeverFetches test:TestDoctorCommitGraphReportsAnUnreadableGraph\n- R4 [satisfied] O passo `Write the Git commit-graph with changed-path filters` nos dois jobs de `.github/workflows/ci.yml` que fazem checkout do histórico inteiro.\n\n### Known gaps\n- Nenhuma.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Final Report\n\n### Delivered scope\n\nNão concluída.\n\n### Residual risks\n\n### Follow-ups\n\n- [open] F1: medir e reduzir o `pose doctor` no harne8, que passa de 900 s em Go, sem processo Git filho, já com o binário anterior a esta spec. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:medium review:2026-11-23)\n\n### Review\n\nRodada 1 (run rrn-237e7d9be5f0c4f5, changes-requested): 4 bloqueadores, corrigidos. F2 a leitura ignorava diretórios de objetos alternativos; F3 preferia a cadeia de camadas ao arquivo único, ao contrário do Git; F4 aceitava cabeçalhos de versão não suportada e arquivos truncados. Os três vinham de reimplementar a leitura do commit-graph; o `doctor` deixou de ler os arquivos e passou a perguntar ao próprio Git: roda `git log -1 -- <path>` com `GIT_TRACE2_EVENT` e procura o evento `bloom`/`statistics` com algum filtro consultado, de modo que vale o grafo que o Git carrega, com as regras dele. O teste cobre um grafo só no alternate (`clone --shared`) e o arquivo único sem filtros ao lado de uma cadeia com filtros (`next`, porque o Git carrega o arquivo único). F5 qualquer erro de leitura suprimia o check; agora só a falta de repositório ou de commit em HEAD o suprime, e as demais falhas viram `warn` com a descrição limitada (`TestDoctorCommitGraphReportsAnUnreadableHistory`, com um commit pai apagado).\n\nRodada 2 (run rrn-c7c3feb56ea14783, recusada porque os ids dos achados novos traziam o prefixo de rodada `R2-`; o rascunho declarou F2 a F4 corrigidos e F5 parcial). Os achados, corrigidos com teste que reprova sem a correção: F6 qualquer falha do primeiro `rev-parse` era tratada como \"não se aplica\"; agora só um diretório que não é repositório (`rev-parse --git-dir` com a mensagem do Git, lida no locale C) e um HEAD que não resolve (saída 1 de `rev-parse --verify --quiet HEAD`) suprimem o check, e um HEAD cujo commit não pode ser lido, ou um repositório que o Git não abre, é `warn` (`TestDoctorCommitGraphTellsUnbornFromBroken`). F7 o caminho sondado era lido como pathspec, e um nome como `*` mudava a busca; agora a busca roda com `GIT_LITERAL_PATHSPECS=1` (`TestDoctorCommitGraphProbesALiteralPath`). F8 com `core.commitGraph=false`, `commitGraph.readChangedPaths=false` ou `commitGraph.changedPathsVersion=0`, reescrever o grafo não mudava a resposta; agora o `doctor` reporta `git.commit-graph-reads` em `warn`, sem correção automática, nomeando a configuração, e não recomenda reescrever o grafo (`TestDoctorCommitGraphNamesDisabledReads`).\n\nRodada 5 (run rrn-6d639d1e28201081, changes-requested; as rodadas 3 e 4 falharam na limpeza do worktree pelo teto de 256 MiB, mas a 3 registrou F9 a F14). Seis bloqueadores, F15 a F20, que reabrem F9 a F14, corrigidos com teste que reprova sem a correção. F15 um clone raso, em que o Git não usa nem escreve commit-graph, recebia uma correção que não resolve; agora não se aplica (`TestDoctorCommitGraphSkipsAShallowClone`). F16 a correção herdava `commitGraph.maxNewFilters`; agora passa `--max-new-filters=-1` (`TestDoctorCommitGraphFixIgnoresMaxNewFilters`). F17 uma árvore de HEAD vazia recomendava reescrever para sempre; agora não se aplica (`TestDoctorCommitGraphSkipsAnEmptyTree`). F18 `readChangedPaths` era lido antes de `changedPathsVersion`, que o Git trata como prioritário; a ordem segue o Git (`TestDoctorCommitGraphFollowsConfigurationPrecedence`). F19 os comandos de diagnóstico podiam buscar objetos num clone parcial; agora rodam com `GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH=1`, e a falta de objetos vira `warn` sem contato com o remoto (`TestDoctorCommitGraphNeverFetches`, que conta os objetos antes e depois). F20 o stderr de um comando bem-sucedido era descartado, e um commit-graph ilegível, que o Git anuncia e contorna, virava recomendação; agora é `warn` com a mensagem do Git (`TestDoctorCommitGraphReportsAnUnreadableGraph`).\n\n     1\tpackage cli\n     2\t\n     3\timport (\n     4\t\t\"bufio\"\n     5\t\t\"bytes\"\n     6\t\t\"encoding/json\"\n     7\t\t\"errors\"\n     8\t\t\"fmt\"\n     9\t\t\"os\"\n    10\t\t\"os/exec\"\n    11\t\t\"strconv\"\n    12\t\t\"strings\"\n    13\t\n    14\t\tposemodel \"github.com/harne8/pose-mcp/internal/pose\"\n    15\t)\n    16\t\n    17\t// commitGraphHistoryThreshold is the history size from which a last-commit\n    18\t// lookup by path is worth accelerating: below it a history walk costs a few\n    19\t// milliseconds (spec pose-doctor-recommends-the-commit-graph).\n    20\tvar commitGraphHistoryThreshold = 500\n    21\t\n    22\t// errCommitGraphNotApplicable marks a root the check does not apply to: not\n    23\t// a Git repository, an unborn HEAD, a shallow history (Git neither reads nor\n    24\t// writes a commit-graph across a shallow boundary), or a HEAD with no file to\n    25\t// look up.\n    26\tvar errCommitGraphNotApplicable = errors.New(\"not a repository whose last-commit lookups a commit-graph can answer\")\n    27\t\n    28\t// commitGraphState is what doctor knows about a repository's commit-graph.\n    29\ttype commitGraphState struct {\n    30\t\tcommits int\n    31\t\t// filtersUsed is Git's own answer: a last-commit lookup by path read\n    32\t\t// changed-path Bloom filters from the commit-graph it loaded.\n    33\t\tfiltersUsed bool\n    34\t\t// readsDisabledBy names the configuration that keeps Git from reading\n    35\t\t// the filters, when the lookup used none.\n    36\t\treadsDisabledBy string\n    37\t}\n    38\t\n    39\t// readCommitGraphState counts HEAD's history and asks Git whether a\n    40\t// last-commit lookup by path uses changed-path Bloom filters. Git reports the\n    41\t// filters it consulted in its trace2 \"bloom\" statistics, so whichever graph it\n    42\t// loads (the object directory's or an alternate's, a single file or a chain,\n    43\t// of any version it accepts) is judged as Git itself uses it. It only reads,\n    44\t// and never fetches: lazy fetching is off, so a partial clone reports the\n    45\t// objects it lacks instead of contacting its remote.\n    46\tfunc readCommitGraphState(root string) (commitGraphState, error) {\n    47\t\tif _, _, err := commitGraphGit(root, nil, \"rev-parse\", \"--git-dir\"); err != nil {\n    48\t\t\tif strings.Contains(err.Error(), \"not a git repository\") {\n    49\t\t\t\treturn commitGraphState{}, errCommitGraphNotApplicable\n    50\t\t\t}\n    51\t\t\treturn commitGraphState{}, fmt.Errorf(\"repository could not be opened: %w\", err)\n    52\t\t}\n    53\t\t// An unborn HEAD names a branch that does not resolve; a HEAD that\n    54\t\t// resolves to a commit Git cannot read is a failure.\n    55\t\tif _, _, err := commitGraphGit(root, nil, \"rev-parse\", \"--verify\", \"--quiet\", \"HEAD\"); err != nil {\n    56\t\t\tvar exit *exec.ExitError\n    57\t\t\tif errors.As(err, &exit) && exit.ExitCode() == 1 {\n    58\t\t\t\treturn commitGraphState{}, errCommitGraphNotApplicable\n    59\t\t\t}\n    60\t\t\treturn commitGraphState{}, fmt.Errorf(\"HEAD could not be read: %w\", err)\n    61\t\t}\n    62\t\tif _, _, err := commitGraphGit(root, nil, \"rev-parse\", \"--verify\", \"HEAD^{commit}\"); err != nil {\n    63\t\t\treturn commitGraphState{}, fmt.Errorf(\"HEAD could not be read: %w\", err)\n    64\t\t}\n    65\t\tshallow, _, err := commitGraphGit(root, nil, \"rev-parse\", \"--is-shallow-repository\")\n    66\t\tif err != nil {\n    67\t\t\treturn commitGraphState{}, fmt.Errorf(\"repository depth could not be read: %w\", err)\n    68\t\t}\n    69\t\tif strings.TrimSpace(shallow) == \"true\" {\n    70\t\t\treturn commitGraphState{}, errCommitGraphNotApplicable\n    71\t\t}\n    72\t\tcount, _, err := commitGraphGit(root, nil, \"rev-list\", \"--count\", \"HEAD\")\n    73\t\tif err != nil {\n    74\t\t\treturn commitGraphState{}, fmt.Errorf(\"history of HEAD could not be counted: %w\", err)\n    75\t\t}\n    76\t\tcommits, err := strconv.Atoi(strings.TrimSpace(count))\n    77\t\tif err != nil {\n    78\t\t\treturn commitGraphState{}, fmt.Errorf(\"history of HEAD could not be counted: %w\", err)\n    79\t\t}\n    80\t\tstate := commitGraphState{commits: commits}\n    81\t\tif commits < commitGraphHistoryThreshold {\n    82\t\t\treturn state, nil\n    83\t\t}\n    84\t\tlisting, _, err := commitGraphGit(root, nil, \"ls-tree\", \"-r\", \"--name-only\", \"-z\", \"HEAD\")\n    85\t\tif err != nil {\n    86\t\t\treturn state, fmt.Errorf(\"files of HEAD could not be listed: %w\", err)\n    87\t\t}\n    88\t\tpath, _, _ := strings.Cut(listing, \"\\x00\")\n    89\t\tif path == \"\" {\n    90\t\t\treturn commitGraphState{}, errCommitGraphNotApplicable\n    91\t\t}\n    92\t\ttrace, err := os.CreateTemp(\"\", \"pose-doctor-trace2-*.json\")\n    93\t\tif err != nil {\n    94\t\t\treturn state, fmt.Errorf(\"Git trace could not be created: %w\", err)\n    95\t\t}\n    96\t\ttracePath := trace.Name()\n    97\t\ttrace.Close()\n    98\t\tdefer os.Remove(tracePath)\n    99\t\t// The path is literal: a name with pathspec magic must not change what\n   100\t\t// Git looks up.\n   101\t\t_, stderr, err := commitGraphGit(root, []string{\"GIT_TRACE2_EVENT=\" + tracePath, \"GIT_LITERAL_PATHSPECS=1\"}, \"log\", \"-1\", \"--format=%H\", \"--\", path)\n   102\t\tif err != nil {\n   103\t\t\treturn state, fmt.Errorf(\"last commit of a file could not be read: %w\", err)\n   104\t\t}\n   105\t\t// Git falls back to a plain walk when its commit-graph cannot be read,\n   106\t\t// and says so on stderr while it succeeds.\n   107\t\tif stderr != \"\" {\n   108\t\t\treturn state, fmt.Errorf(\"Git reported a problem while reading history: %s\", stderr)\n   109\t\t}\n   110\t\traw, err := os.ReadFile(tracePath)\n   111\t\tif err != nil {\n   112\t\t\treturn state, fmt.Errorf(\"Git trace could not be read: %w\", err)\n   113\t\t}\n   114\t\tstate.filtersUsed = traceUsedBloomFilters(raw)\n   115\t\tif !state.filtersUsed {\n   116\t\t\tstate.readsDisabledBy = commitGraphReadsDisabledBy(root)\n   117\t\t}\n   118\t\treturn state, nil\n   119\t}\n   120\t\n   121\t// traceUsedBloomFilters reports whether a trace2 event stream carries a\n   122\t// \"bloom\" statistics event in which some filter answered a lookup.\n   123\tfunc traceUsedBloomFilters(raw []byte) bool {\n   124\t\tscanner := bufio.NewScanner(bytes.NewReader(raw))\n   125\t\tscanner.Buffer(make([]byte, 0, 64<<10), 1<<20)\n   126\t\tfor scanner.Scan() {\n   127\t\t\tvar event struct {\n   128\t\t\t\tCategory string `json:\"category\"`\n   129\t\t\t\tKey      string `json:\"key\"`\n   130\t\t\t\tValue    struct {\n   131\t\t\t\t\tMaybe         int `json:\"maybe\"`\n   132\t\t\t\t\tDefinitelyNot int `json:\"definitely_not\"`\n   133\t\t\t\t} `json:\"value\"`\n   134\t\t\t}\n   135\t\t\tif json.Unmarshal(scanner.Bytes(), &event) != nil {\n   136\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   137\t\t\t}\n   138\t\t\tif event.Category == \"bloom\" && event.Key == \"statistics\" && event.Value.Maybe+event.Value.DefinitelyNot > 0 {\n   139\t\t\t\treturn true\n   140\t\t\t}\n   141\t\t}\n   142\t\treturn false\n   143\t}\n   144\t\n   145\t// commitGraphReadsDisabledBy names the configuration that keeps Git from\n   146\t// reading a commit-graph or its changed-path filters, or \"\" when none does:\n   147\t// with it set, writing the graph cannot change the answer. Precedence follows\n   148\t// Git: commitGraph.changedPathsVersion, when set, overrides the deprecated\n   149\t// commitGraph.readChangedPaths.\n   150\tfunc commitGraphReadsDisabledBy(root string) string {\n   151\t\tget := func(kind, key string) (string, bool) {\n   152\t\t\tout, _, err := commitGraphGit(root, nil, \"config\", \"--type=\"+kind, \"--get\", key)\n   153\t\t\tvalue := strings.TrimSpace(out)\n   154\t\t\treturn value, err == nil && value != \"\"\n   155\t\t}\n   156\t\tif value, ok := get(\"bool\", \"core.commitGraph\"); ok && value == \"false\" {\n   157\t\t\treturn \"core.commitGraph=false\"\n   158\t\t}\n   159\t\tif value, ok := get(\"int\", \"commitGraph.changedPathsVersion\"); ok {\n   160\t\t\tif value == \"0\" {\n   161\t\t\t\treturn \"commitGraph.changedPathsVersion=0\"\n   162\t\t\t}\n   163\t\t\treturn \"\"\n   164\t\t}\n   165\t\tif value, ok := get(\"bool\", \"commitGraph.readChangedPaths\"); ok && value == \"false\" {\n   166\t\t\treturn \"commitGraph.readChangedPaths=false\"\n   167\t\t}\n   168\t\treturn \"\"\n   169\t}\n   170\t\n   171\t// writeCommitGraph writes the repository's commit-graph with changed-path\n   172\t// Bloom filters for every commit, whatever commitGraph.maxNewFilters says;\n   173\t// it only writes under the Git object directory.\n   174\tfunc writeCommitGraph(root string) error {\n   175\t\t_, _, err := commitGraphGit(root, nil, \"commit-graph\", \"write\", \"--reachable\", \"--changed-paths\", \"--max-new-filters=-1\")\n   176\t\treturn err\n   177\t}\n   178\t\n   179\t// commitGraphGit runs Git in root, without lazy fetching and in the C\n   180\t// locale, with extra environment; it returns stdout and stderr, and a\n   181\t// failure carries the stderr, bounded.\n   182\tfunc commitGraphGit(root string, env []string, args ...string) (string, string, error) {\n   183\t\tcmd := posemodel.RawHistoryGit(root, args...)\n   184\t\t// Git's messages are read below; they are read in the C locale. A\n   185\t\t// diagnostic never contacts a remote.\n   186\t\tcmd.Env = append(append(cmd.Env, \"LC_ALL=C\", \"LANGUAGE=C\", \"GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH=1\"), env...)\n   187\t\tvar stderr bytes.Buffer\n   188\t\tcmd.Stderr = &stderr\n   189\t\tout, err := cmd.Output()\n   190\t\tdetail := strings.TrimSpace(stderr.String())\n   191\t\tif len(detail) > 200 {\n   192\t\t\tdetail = detail[:200] + \"…\"\n   193\t\t}\n   194\t\tif err != nil {\n   195\t\t\treturn string(out), detail, &commitGraphGitError{args: args[0], err: err, detail: detail}\n   196\t\t}\n   197\t\treturn string(out), detail, nil\n   198\t}\n   199\t\n   200\t// commitGraphGitError is a failed Git command with its stderr, bounded; it\n   201\t// unwraps to the command's error, an *exec.ExitError when Git ran.\n   202\ttype commitGraphGitError struct {\n   203\t\targs   string\n   204\t\terr    error\n   205\t\tdetail string\n   206\t}\n   207\t\n   208\tfunc (e *commitGraphGitError) Error() string {\n   209\t\tif e.detail == \"\" {\n   210\t\t\treturn \"git \" + e.args + \" \" + e.err.Error()\n   211\t\t}\n   212\t\treturn \"git \" + e.args + \": \" + e.err.Error() + \" \" + e.detail\n   213\t}\n   214\t\n   215\tfunc (e *commitGraphGitError) Unwrap() error { return e.err }\n     1\tpackage cli\n     2\t\n     3\timport (\n     4\t\t\"bytes\"\n     5\t\t\"encoding/json\"\n     6\t\t\"errors\"\n     7\t\t\"os\"\n     8\t\t\"os/exec\"\n     9\t\t\"path/filepath\"\n    10\t\t\"strings\"\n    11\t\t\"testing\"\n    12\t)\n    13\t\n    14\tfunc doctorCommitGraphFinding(t *testing.T, repo string) doctorFinding {\n    15\t\tt.Helper()\n    16\t\tvar finding doctorFinding\n    17\t\tinDir(t, repo, func() {\n    18\t\t\tvar out, errB bytes.Buffer\n    19\t\t\tMain([]string{\"doctor\", \"--json\"}, &out, &errB)\n    20\t\t\tvar report doctorJSON\n    21\t\t\tif err := json.Unmarshal(out.Bytes(), &report); err != nil {\n    22\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"invalid JSON: %v\\n%s\", err, out.String())\n    23\t\t\t}\n    24\t\t\tfor _, f := range report.Findings {\n    25\t\t\t\tif f.Check == \"git.commit-graph\" {\n    26\t\t\t\t\tfinding = f\n    27\t\t\t\t}\n    28\t\t\t}\n    29\t\t})\n    30\t\tif finding.Check == \"\" {\n    31\t\t\tt.Fatal(\"doctor reported no git.commit-graph check\")\n    32\t\t}\n    33\t\treturn finding\n    34\t}\n    35\t\n    36\tfunc gitInRepo(t *testing.T, repo string, args ...string) {\n    37\t\tt.Helper()\n    38\t\tif out, err := exec.Command(\"git\", append([]string{\"-C\", repo}, args...)...).CombinedOutput(); err != nil {\n    39\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"git %v: %v %s\", args, err, out)\n    40\t\t}\n    41\t}\n    42\t\n    43\tfunc removeCommitGraph(t *testing.T, repo string) {\n    44\t\tt.Helper()\n    45\t\tinfo := filepath.Join(repo, \".git\", \"objects\", \"info\")\n    46\t\tfor _, name := range []string{\"commit-graph\", \"commit-graphs\"} {\n    47\t\t\tif err := os.RemoveAll(filepath.Join(info, name)); err != nil {\n    48\t\t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n    49\t\t\t}\n    50\t\t}\n    51\t}\n    52\t\n    53\t// Spec pose-doctor-recommends-the-commit-graph: R1 a long history Git walks\n    54\t// whole is a next step with a fix; R2 the fix writes the filters and the\n    55\t// check turns ok; R3 a short history needs none. The answer is Git's own, so\n    56\t// it follows whichever graph Git loads.\n    57\tfunc TestDoctorRecommendsTheCommitGraph(t *testing.T) {\n    58\t\trepo := doctorFixture(t)\n    59\t\toriginal := commitGraphHistoryThreshold\n    60\t\tt.Cleanup(func() { commitGraphHistoryThreshold = original })\n    61\t\tfor i := 0; i < 4; i++ {\n    62\t\t\t// Each commit changes a file of its own, so a lookup of another path\n    63\t\t\t// has commits the filters can rule out.\n    64\t\t\tif err := os.WriteFile(filepath.Join(repo, \"zz-history.txt\"), []byte(strings.Repeat(\"x\", i+1)), 0o644); err != nil {\n    65\t\t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n    66\t\t\t}\n    67\t\t\tgitInRepo(t, repo, \"add\", \"zz-history.txt\")\n    68\t\t\tgitInRepo(t, repo, \"-c\", \"user.name=fixture\", \"-c\", \"user.email=fixture@example.invalid\", \"-c\", \"commit.gpgsign=false\", \"commit\", \"-q\", \"-m\", \"history\")\n    69\t\t}\n    70\t\tremoveCommitGraph(t, repo)\n    71\t\n    72\t\tcommitGraphHistoryThreshold = 1 << 30\n    73\t\tif f := doctorCommitGraphFinding(t, repo); f.Level != \"ok\" {\n    74\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"a short history is not ok: %+v\", f)\n    75\t\t}\n    76\t\n    77\t\tcommitGraphHistoryThreshold = 3\n    78\t\tmissing := doctorCommitGraphFinding(t, repo)\n    79\t\tif missing.Level != \"next\" || missing.FixCode != \"git.commit-graph\" || missing.RemediationClass != remediationFixable {\n    80\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"a long history without a commit-graph: %+v\", missing)\n    81\t\t}\n    82\t\n    83\t\tinDir(t, repo, func() {\n    84\t\t\tvar out, errB bytes.Buffer\n    85\t\t\tMain([]string{\"doctor\", \"--fix\", \"--yes\", \"--only\", \"git.commit-graph\"}, &out, &errB)\n    86\t\t})\n    87\t\tif fixed := doctorCommitGraphFinding(t, repo); fixed.Level != \"ok\" {\n    88\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"the fix did not satisfy the check: %+v\", fixed)\n    89\t\t}\n    90\t\n    91\t\tremoveCommitGraph(t, repo)\n    92\t\tgitInRepo(t, repo, \"commit-graph\", \"write\", \"--reachable\", \"--no-changed-paths\")\n    93\t\tif plain := doctorCommitGraphFinding(t, repo); plain.Level != \"next\" {\n    94\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"a commit-graph without changed-path filters is not recommended again: %+v\", plain)\n    95\t\t}\n    96\t\n    97\t\tremoveCommitGraph(t, repo)\n    98\t\tgitInRepo(t, repo, \"commit-graph\", \"write\", \"--reachable\", \"--changed-paths\", \"--split\")\n    99\t\tif split := doctorCommitGraphFinding(t, repo); split.Level != \"ok\" {\n   100\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"a split commit-graph with changed paths is not recognized: %+v\", split)\n   101\t\t}\n   102\t\n   103\t\t// Review F3: with a single graph and a chain, Git loads the single graph.\n   104\t\tgitInRepo(t, repo, \"commit-graph\", \"write\", \"--reachable\", \"--no-changed-paths\")\n   105\t\tif both := doctorCommitGraphFinding(t, repo); both.Level != \"next\" {\n   106\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"an unfiltered single graph beside a filtered chain is judged by the chain: %+v\", both)\n   107\t\t}\n   108\t\tremoveCommitGraph(t, repo)\n   109\t\tgitInRepo(t, repo, \"commit-graph\", \"write\", \"--reachable\", \"--changed-paths\")\n   110\t\n   111\t\t// Review F2: a repository whose graph lives only in an alternate.\n   112\t\tshared := filepath.Join(t.TempDir(), \"shared\")\n   113\t\tif out, err := exec.Command(\"git\", \"clone\", \"-q\", \"--shared\", repo, shared).CombinedOutput(); err != nil {\n   114\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"clone --shared: %v %s\", err, out)\n   115\t\t}\n   116\t\tremoveCommitGraph(t, shared)\n   117\t\tstate, err := readCommitGraphState(shared)\n   118\t\tif err != nil || !state.filtersUsed {\n   119\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"a graph in an alternate is not seen: %+v %v\", state, err)\n   120\t\t}\n   121\t}\n   122\t\n   123\t// Review F5: a repository whose history cannot be read is a warning, not a\n   124\t// silent pass; a root that is not a repository gets no check.\n   125\tfunc TestDoctorCommitGraphReportsAnUnreadableHistory(t *testing.T) {\n   126\t\tif _, err := readCommitGraphState(t.TempDir()); !errors.Is(err, errCommitGraphNotApplicable) {\n   127\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"a directory outside Git: %v, want not applicable\", err)\n   128\t\t}\n   129\t\trepo := doctorFixture(t)\n   130\t\toriginal := commitGraphHistoryThreshold\n   131\t\tt.Cleanup(func() { commitGraphHistoryThreshold = original })\n   132\t\tcommitGraphHistoryThreshold = 1\n   133\t\tcommit := func() {\n   134\t\t\tgitInRepo(t, repo, \"-c\", \"user.name=fixture\", \"-c\", \"user.email=fixture@example.invalid\", \"-c\", \"commit.gpgsign=false\", \"commit\", \"-q\", \"--allow-empty\", \"-m\", \"history\")\n   135\t\t}\n   136\t\tcommit()\n   137\t\tcommit()\n   138\t\tout, err := exec.Command(\"git\", \"-C\", repo, \"rev-parse\", \"HEAD~1\").Output()\n   139\t\tif err != nil {\n   140\t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n   141\t\t}\n   142\t\tparent := strings.TrimSpace(string(out))\n   143\t\tif err := os.Remove(filepath.Join(repo, \".git\", \"objects\", parent[:2], parent[2:])); err != nil {\n   144\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"the parent commit is not a loose object: %v\", err)\n   145\t\t}\n   146\t\tif f := doctorCommitGraphFinding(t, repo); f.Level != \"warn\" || !strings.Contains(f.Message, \"could not be read\") {\n   147\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"an unreadable history: %+v\", f)\n   148\t\t}\n   149\t}\n   150\t\n   151\t// longHistoryRepo is an installed repository with commits that each change a\n   152\t// file of their own, the threshold lowered under them, and its commit-graph\n   153\t// written with changed-path filters.\n   154\tfunc longHistoryRepo(t *testing.T, extra func(repo string)) string {\n   155\t\tt.Helper()\n   156\t\trepo := doctorFixture(t)\n   157\t\toriginal := commitGraphHistoryThreshold\n   158\t\tt.Cleanup(func() { commitGraphHistoryThreshold = original })\n   159\t\tcommitGraphHistoryThreshold = 3\n   160\t\tif extra != nil {\n   161\t\t\textra(repo)\n   162\t\t}\n   163\t\tfor i := 0; i < 4; i++ {\n   164\t\t\tif err := os.WriteFile(filepath.Join(repo, \"zz-history.txt\"), []byte(strings.Repeat(\"x\", i+1)), 0o644); err != nil {\n   165\t\t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n   166\t\t\t}\n   167\t\t\tgitInRepo(t, repo, \"add\", \"zz-history.txt\")\n   168\t\t\tgitInRepo(t, repo, \"-c\", \"user.name=fixture\", \"-c\", \"user.email=fixture@example.invalid\", \"-c\", \"commit.gpgsign=false\", \"commit\", \"-q\", \"-m\", \"history\")\n   169\t\t}\n   170\t\tremoveCommitGraph(t, repo)\n   171\t\tgitInRepo(t, repo, \"commit-graph\", \"write\", \"--reachable\", \"--changed-paths\")\n   172\t\treturn repo\n   173\t}\n   174\t\n   175\t// Review F6: an unborn HEAD is not applicable, but a repository Git cannot\n   176\t// open is reported.\n   177\tfunc TestDoctorCommitGraphTellsUnbornFromBroken(t *testing.T) {\n   178\t\tunborn := t.TempDir()\n   179\t\tgitInRepo(t, unborn, \"init\", \"-q\")\n   180\t\tif _, err := readCommitGraphState(unborn); !errors.Is(err, errCommitGraphNotApplicable) {\n   181\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"an unborn HEAD: %v, want not applicable\", err)\n   182\t\t}\n   183\t\tbroken := longHistoryRepo(t, nil)\n   184\t\tgitInRepo(t, broken, \"config\", \"core.bare\", \"invalid\")\n   185\t\tif _, err := readCommitGraphState(broken); err == nil || errors.Is(err, errCommitGraphNotApplicable) {\n   186\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"a repository with an invalid configuration: %v, want a reported failure\", err)\n   187\t\t}\n   188\t\theadless := longHistoryRepo(t, nil)\n   189\t\tout, err := exec.Command(\"git\", \"-C\", headless, \"rev-parse\", \"HEAD\").Output()\n   190\t\tif err != nil {\n   191\t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n   192\t\t}\n   193\t\thead := strings.TrimSpace(string(out))\n   194\t\tif err := os.Remove(filepath.Join(headless, \".git\", \"objects\", head[:2], head[2:])); err != nil {\n   195\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"the HEAD commit is not a loose object: %v\", err)\n   196\t\t}\n   197\t\tremoveCommitGraph(t, headless)\n   198\t\tif _, err := readCommitGraphState(headless); err == nil || errors.Is(err, errCommitGraphNotApplicable) {\n   199\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"a HEAD whose commit is missing: %v, want a reported failure\", err)\n   200\t\t}\n   201\t}\n   202\t\n   203\t// Review F7: a first file whose name is pathspec syntax is looked up as the\n   204\t// literal name, so the filters still answer.\n   205\tfunc TestDoctorCommitGraphProbesALiteralPath(t *testing.T) {\n   206\t\trepo := longHistoryRepo(t, func(repo string) {\n   207\t\t\tif err := os.WriteFile(filepath.Join(repo, \"*\"), []byte(\"star\\n\"), 0o644); err != nil {\n   208\t\t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n   209\t\t\t}\n   210\t\t\tgitInRepo(t, repo, \"add\", \"--\", \"*\")\n   211\t\t\tgitInRepo(t, repo, \"-c\", \"user.name=fixture\", \"-c\", \"user.email=fixture@example.invalid\", \"-c\", \"commit.gpgsign=false\", \"commit\", \"-q\", \"-m\", \"star\")\n   212\t\t})\n   213\t\tout, err := exec.Command(\"git\", \"-C\", repo, \"ls-tree\", \"-r\", \"--name-only\", \"HEAD\").Output()\n   214\t\tif err != nil || !strings.HasPrefix(string(out), \"*\\n\") {\n   215\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"the fixture's first path is not '*': %q %v\", out, err)\n   216\t\t}\n   217\t\tstate, err := readCommitGraphState(repo)\n   218\t\tif err != nil || !state.filtersUsed {\n   219\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"a filtered graph probed through a pathspec-like name: %+v %v\", state, err)\n   220\t\t}\n   221\t}\n   222\t\n   223\t// Review F8: configuration that keeps Git from reading the filters is a\n   224\t// warning that names it, not a graph rewrite that cannot help.\n   225\tfunc TestDoctorCommitGraphNamesDisabledReads(t *testing.T) {\n   226\t\trepo := longHistoryRepo(t, nil)\n   227\t\tgitInRepo(t, repo, \"config\", \"commitGraph.changedPathsVersion\", \"0\")\n   228\t\tvar reads doctorFinding\n   229\t\tinDir(t, repo, func() {\n   230\t\t\tvar out, errB bytes.Buffer\n   231\t\t\tMain([]string{\"doctor\", \"--json\"}, &out, &errB)\n   232\t\t\tvar report doctorJSON\n   233\t\t\tif err := json.Unmarshal(out.Bytes(), &report); err != nil {\n   234\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"invalid JSON: %v\", err)\n   235\t\t\t}\n   236\t\t\tfor _, f := range report.Findings {\n   237\t\t\t\tif f.Check == \"git.commit-graph\" {\n   238\t\t\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"the graph rewrite is recommended although configuration disables reading it: %+v\", f)\n   239\t\t\t\t}\n   240\t\t\t\tif f.Check == \"git.commit-graph-reads\" {\n   241\t\t\t\t\treads = f\n   242\t\t\t\t}\n   243\t\t\t}\n   244\t\t})\n   245\t\tif reads.Level != \"warn\" || !strings.Contains(reads.Message, \"commitGraph.changedPathsVersion=0\") || reads.FixCode != \"\" {\n   246\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"disabled filter reads: %+v\", reads)\n   247\t\t}\n   248\t}\n   249\t\n   250\t// Review F15: a shallow clone, whose history Git cannot put in a\n   251\t// commit-graph, gets no recommendation it cannot satisfy.\n   252\tfunc TestDoctorCommitGraphSkipsAShallowClone(t *testing.T) {\n   253\t\trepo := longHistoryRepo(t, nil)\n   254\t\tshallow := filepath.Join(t.TempDir(), \"shallow\")\n   255\t\tif out, err := exec.Command(\"git\", \"clone\", \"-q\", \"--depth\", \"4\", \"file://\"+repo, shallow).CombinedOutput(); err != nil {\n   256\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"shallow clone: %v %s\", err, out)\n   257\t\t}\n   258\t\tif _, err := readCommitGraphState(shallow); !errors.Is(err, errCommitGraphNotApplicable) {\n   259\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"a shallow clone: %v, want not applicable\", err)\n   260\t\t}\n   261\t}\n   262\t\n   263\t// Review F16: the fix writes filters for every commit even when\n   264\t// commitGraph.maxNewFilters would allow none.\n   265\tfunc TestDoctorCommitGraphFixIgnoresMaxNewFilters(t *testing.T) {\n   266\t\trepo := longHistoryRepo(t, nil)\n   267\t\tgitInRepo(t, repo, \"config\", \"commitGraph.maxNewFilters\", \"0\")\n   268\t\tremoveCommitGraph(t, repo)\n   269\t\tif err := writeCommitGraph(repo); err != nil {\n   270\t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n   271\t\t}\n   272\t\tstate, err := readCommitGraphState(repo)\n   273\t\tif err != nil || !state.filtersUsed {\n   274\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"the fix under maxNewFilters=0: %+v %v\", state, err)\n   275\t\t}\n   276\t}\n   277\t\n   278\t// Review F17: a HEAD with no file to look up is not applicable, not a\n   279\t// rewrite recommended forever.\n   280\tfunc TestDoctorCommitGraphSkipsAnEmptyTree(t *testing.T) {\n   281\t\trepo := longHistoryRepo(t, nil)\n   282\t\tgitInRepo(t, repo, \"rm\", \"-q\", \"-r\", \"--\", \".\")\n   283\t\tgitInRepo(t, repo, \"-c\", \"user.name=fixture\", \"-c\", \"user.email=fixture@example.invalid\", \"-c\", \"commit.gpgsign=false\", \"commit\", \"-q\", \"-m\", \"empty\")\n   284\t\tif _, err := readCommitGraphState(repo); !errors.Is(err, errCommitGraphNotApplicable) {\n   285\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"an empty HEAD tree: %v, want not applicable\", err)\n   286\t\t}\n   287\t}\n   288\t\n   289\t// Review F18: commitGraph.changedPathsVersion overrides the deprecated\n   290\t// readChangedPaths, so a missing graph is still a fixable recommendation.\n   291\tfunc TestDoctorCommitGraphFollowsConfigurationPrecedence(t *testing.T) {\n   292\t\trepo := longHistoryRepo(t, nil)\n   293\t\tgitInRepo(t, repo, \"config\", \"commitGraph.readChangedPaths\", \"false\")\n   294\t\tgitInRepo(t, repo, \"config\", \"commitGraph.changedPathsVersion\", \"1\")\n   295\t\tremoveCommitGraph(t, repo)\n   296\t\tif f := doctorCommitGraphFinding(t, repo); f.Level != \"next\" || f.FixCode != \"git.commit-graph\" {\n   297\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"a missing graph under changedPathsVersion=1 and readChangedPaths=false: %+v\", f)\n   298\t\t}\n   299\t}\n   300\t\n   301\t// Review F19: in a partial clone that lacks trees, the diagnosis fails\n   302\t// without fetching anything from the remote.\n   303\tfunc TestDoctorCommitGraphNeverFetches(t *testing.T) {\n   304\t\trepo := longHistoryRepo(t, nil)\n   305\t\tgitInRepo(t, repo, \"config\", \"uploadpack.allowFilter\", \"true\")\n   306\t\tpartial := filepath.Join(t.TempDir(), \"partial\")\n   307\t\tif out, err := exec.Command(\"git\", \"clone\", \"-q\", \"--no-checkout\", \"--filter=tree:0\", \"file://\"+repo, partial).CombinedOutput(); err != nil {\n   308\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"partial clone: %v %s\", err, out)\n   309\t\t}\n   310\t\tobjects := func() string {\n   311\t\t\tout, err := exec.Command(\"git\", \"-C\", partial, \"count-objects\", \"-v\").Output()\n   312\t\t\tif err != nil {\n   313\t\t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n   314\t\t\t}\n   315\t\t\treturn string(out)\n   316\t\t}\n   317\t\tbefore := objects()\n   318\t\toriginal := commitGraphHistoryThreshold\n   319\t\tcommitGraphHistoryThreshold = 1\n   320\t\tt.Cleanup(func() { commitGraphHistoryThreshold = original })\n   321\t\tif _, err := readCommitGraphState(partial); err == nil || errors.Is(err, errCommitGraphNotApplicable) {\n   322\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"a partial clone without its trees: %v, want a reported failure\", err)\n   323\t\t}\n   324\t\tif after := objects(); after != before {\n   325\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"the diagnosis fetched objects:\\nbefore %s\\nafter %s\", before, after)\n   326\t\t}\n   327\t}\n   328\t\n   329\t// Review F20: a commit-graph Git cannot read, which it reports on stderr\n   330\t// while falling back to a plain walk, is a warning, not a rewrite.\n   331\tfunc TestDoctorCommitGraphReportsAnUnreadableGraph(t *testing.T) {\n   332\t\trepo := longHistoryRepo(t, nil)\n   333\t\tgraph := filepath.Join(repo, \".git\", \"objects\", \"info\", \"commit-graph\")\n   334\t\tremoveCommitGraph(t, repo)\n   335\t\tif err := os.WriteFile(graph, []byte(\"CGPH\\x01\\x01\\x05\\x00garbage\"), 0o444); err != nil {\n   336\t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n   337\t\t}\n   338\t\tif f := doctorCommitGraphFinding(t, repo); f.Level != \"warn\" {\n   339\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"an unreadable commit-graph: %+v\", f)\n   340\t\t}\n   341\t}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '121,170p' pose-mcp/internal/cli/doctor_commit_graph.go; git diff 2bf2adf..8cb2690 -- pose-mcp/internal/cli/doctor.go .github/workflows/ci.yml .pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json; cat /var/tmp/closeout/ac-dc.out /var/tmp/closeout/sc-dc.out; pose suggest review --path pose-mcp; rg -n 'commit.graph|commit-graph|trace2' .pose/knowledge; rg -n 'func RawHistoryGit|func gitCommand|CommandContext' pose-mcp/internal/pose/git*; cat .pose/rules/documentation-style.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '121,170p' pose-mcp/internal/cli/doctor_commit_graph.go; git diff 2bf2adf..8cb2690 -- pose-mcp/internal/cli/doctor.go .github/workflows/ci.yml .pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json; cat /var/tmp/closeout/ac-dc.out /var/tmp/closeout/sc-dc.out; pose suggest review --path pose-mcp; rg -n 'commit.graph|commit-graph|trace2' .pose/knowledge; rg -n 'func RawHistoryGit|func gitCommand|CommandContext' pose-mcp/internal/pose/git*; cat .pose/rules/documentation-style.md\"","aggregated_output":"// traceUsedBloomFilters reports whether a trace2 event stream carries a\n// \"bloom\" statistics event in which some filter answered a lookup.\nfunc traceUsedBloomFilters(raw []byte) bool {\n\tscanner := bufio.NewScanner(bytes.NewReader(raw))\n\tscanner.Buffer(make([]byte, 0, 64<<10), 1<<20)\n\tfor scanner.Scan() {\n\t\tvar event struct {\n\t\t\tCategory string `json:\"category\"`\n\t\t\tKey      string `json:\"key\"`\n\t\t\tValue    struct {\n\t\t\t\tMaybe         int `json:\"maybe\"`\n\t\t\t\tDefinitelyNot int `json:\"definitely_not\"`\n\t\t\t} `json:\"value\"`\n\t\t}\n\t\tif json.Unmarshal(scanner.Bytes(), &event) != nil {\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tif event.Category == \"bloom\" && event.Key == \"statistics\" && event.Value.Maybe+event.Value.DefinitelyNot > 0 {\n\t\t\treturn true\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn false\n}\n\n// commitGraphReadsDisabledBy names the configuration that keeps Git from\n// reading a commit-graph or its changed-path filters, or \"\" when none does:\n// with it set, writing the graph cannot change the answer. Precedence follows\n// Git: commitGraph.changedPathsVersion, when set, overrides the deprecated\n// commitGraph.readChangedPaths.\nfunc commitGraphReadsDisabledBy(root string) string {\n\tget := func(kind, key string) (string, bool) {\n\t\tout, _, err := commitGraphGit(root, nil, \"config\", \"--type=\"+kind, \"--get\", key)\n\t\tvalue := strings.TrimSpace(out)\n\t\treturn value, err == nil && value != \"\"\n\t}\n\tif value, ok := get(\"bool\", \"core.commitGraph\"); ok && value == \"false\" {\n\t\treturn \"core.commitGraph=false\"\n\t}\n\tif value, ok := get(\"int\", \"commitGraph.changedPathsVersion\"); ok {\n\t\tif value == \"0\" {\n\t\t\treturn \"commitGraph.changedPathsVersion=0\"\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn \"\"\n\t}\n\tif value, ok := get(\"bool\", \"commitGraph.readChangedPaths\"); ok && value == \"false\" {\n\t\treturn \"commitGraph.readChangedPaths=false\"\n\t}\n\treturn \"\"\n}\n\ndiff --git a/.github/workflows/ci.yml b/.github/workflows/ci.yml\nindex 8512af6c..cdebba85 100644\n--- a/.github/workflows/ci.yml\n+++ b/.github/workflows/ci.yml\n@@ -18,6 +18,12 @@ jobs:\n       # runner where it matters (spec pose-release-boundary-rehearsal).\n       - uses: actions/checkout@3d3c42e5aac5ba805825da76410c181273ba90b1 # v7.0.1\n         with: { fetch-depth: 0 }\n+      # Governance reads ask Git for the last commit that touched each\n+      # artifact; on the full history each lookup walks it. The commit-graph\n+      # with changed-path filters answers from the filters (47 ms -> 2 ms a\n+      # lookup; spec pose-doctor-recommends-the-commit-graph).\n+      - name: Write the Git commit-graph with changed-path filters\n+        run: git commit-graph write --reachable --changed-paths\n       - uses: actions/setup-go@b7ad1dad31e06c5925ef5d2fc7ad053ef454303e # v7.0.0\n         with: { go-version: \"1.26.10\", cache: true, cache-dependency-path: pose-mcp/go.mod }\n       - name: Go tests (engine drift guard included)\n@@ -117,6 +123,12 @@ jobs:\n       # exactly this reason, reporting a governance defect that did not exist.\n       - uses: actions/checkout@3d3c42e5aac5ba805825da76410c181273ba90b1 # v7.0.1\n         with: { fetch-depth: 0 }\n+      # Governance reads ask Git for the last commit that touched each\n+      # artifact; on the full history each lookup walks it. The commit-graph\n+      # with changed-path filters answers from the filters (47 ms -> 2 ms a\n+      # lookup; spec pose-doctor-recommends-the-commit-graph).\n+      - name: Write the Git commit-graph with changed-path filters\n+        run: git commit-graph write --reachable --changed-paths\n       - uses: actions/setup-go@b7ad1dad31e06c5925ef5d2fc7ad053ef454303e # v7.0.0\n         with: { go-version: \"1.26.10\", cache: true, cache-dependency-path: pose-mcp/go.mod }\n       - name: Build development pose binary\ndiff --git a/.pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json b/.pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json\nindex 966572c1..3263dc8a 100644\n--- a/.pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json\n+++ b/.pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json\n@@ -2419,10 +2419,24 @@\n           \"severity\": \"required\",\n           \"evidenceClass\": \"integration\"\n         },\n+        {\n+          \"name\": \"git-snapshot-budget-scales-with-the-tree-integration\",\n+          \"program\": \"go\",\n+          \"args\": [\"test\", \"./internal/pose\", \"-run\", \"TestGitSnapshotBudget|TestReviewWorktreeCleanup|TestGitTreeListingIsBounded\", \"-count=1\"],\n+          \"severity\": \"required\",\n+          \"evidenceClass\": \"integration\"\n+        },\n+        {\n+          \"name\": \"doctor-recommends-the-commit-graph-integration\",\n+          \"program\": \"go\",\n+          \"args\": [\"test\", \"./internal/cli\", \"-run\", \"TestDoctorRecommendsTheCommitGraph|TestDoctorCommitGraph\", \"-count=1\"],\n+          \"severity\": \"required\",\n+          \"evidenceClass\": \"integration\"\n+        },\n         {\n           \"name\": \"review-ledger-is-read-once-per-operation-integration\",\n           \"program\": \"go\",\n-          \"args\": [\"test\", \"./internal/pose\", \"-run\", \"TestReviewLedgerIsReadOncePerOperation|TestReviewLedgerWithoutAnOperationIsReadEveryTime|TestReviewLedgerMemoAnswersAsAFreshRead|TestReviewLedgerMemoComputesOnceForConcurrentMisses|TestReviewLedgerMemoGivesIsolatedCopies|TestCopyReviewRunsCoversEveryUnexportedField\", \"-count=1\"],\n+          \"args\": [\"test\", \"./internal/pose\", \"-run\", \"TestReviewLedgerIsReadOncePerOperation|TestReviewLedgerWithoutAnOperationIsReadEveryTime|TestReviewLedgerMemoAnswersAsAFreshRead|TestReviewLedgerMemoComputesOnceForConcurrentMisses|TestReviewLedgerMemoGivesIsolatedCopies|TestCopyReviewRunsCoversEveryUnexportedField|TestReviewLedgerMemoIsNotServedAfterTheOperationEnds|TestReviewLedgerMemoRefusalsStayVisible|TestReviewLedgerMemoAttributesEveryConsumingProducer\", \"-count=1\"],\n           \"severity\": \"required\",\n           \"evidenceClass\": \"integration\"\n         },\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/doctor.go b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/doctor.go\nindex d091206a..e7d32771 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/doctor.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/doctor.go\n@@ -9,6 +9,7 @@ import (\n \t\"bytes\"\n \t\"context\"\n \t\"encoding/json\"\n+\t\"errors\"\n \t\"fmt\"\n \t\"io\"\n \t\"io/fs\"\n@@ -89,6 +90,10 @@ var doctorFixRegistry = map[string]doctorFix{\n \t\t\treturn err\n \t\t},\n \t},\n+\t\"git.commit-graph\": {\n+\t\tdescribe: \"write the Git commit-graph with changed-path filters (git commit-graph write --reachable --changed-paths)\",\n+\t\tapply:    writeCommitGraph,\n+\t},\n \t\"skills.symlinks\": {\n \t\tdescribe: \"recreate .claude/skills symlinks\",\n \t\tapply: func(root string) error {\n@@ -355,6 +360,25 @@ func runDoctorDiagnostics(locale cliLocale) (root string, findings []doctorFindi\n \t\tadd(\"hooks.pre-commit\", \"ok\", text(\"pre-commit hook installed\", \"pre-commit instalado\"), \"\")\n \t}\n \n+\t// 7b. Git commit-graph. Governance reads ask Git for the last commit that\n+\t// touched each artifact; on a long history each lookup walks it, and a\n+\t// commit-graph with changed-path filters answers it from the filters\n+\t// (spec pose-doctor-recommends-the-commit-graph).\n+\tgraph, graphErr := readCommitGraphState(root)\n+\tswitch {\n+\tcase errors.Is(graphErr, errCommitGraphNotApplicable):\n+\tcase graphErr != nil:\n+\t\tadd(\"git.commit-graph\", \"warn\", text(\"Git commit-graph state could not be read: \"+graphErr.Error(), \"estado do commit-graph do Git não pôde ser lido: \"+graphErr.Error()), text(\"check that the repository and its object directory are readable\", \"confira se o repositório e o diretório de objetos podem ser lidos\"))\n+\tcase graph.commits < commitGraphHistoryThreshold:\n+\t\tadd(\"git.commit-graph\", \"ok\", text(fmt.Sprintf(\"history of %d commits does not need a commit-graph\", graph.commits), fmt.Sprintf(\"histórico de %d commits não precisa de commit-graph\", graph.commits)), \"\")\n+\tcase graph.readsDisabledBy != \"\":\n+\t\tadd(\"git.commit-graph-reads\", \"warn\", text(fmt.Sprintf(\"Git configuration %s keeps last-commit lookups over a history of %d commits from reading changed-path filters\", graph.readsDisabledBy, graph.commits), fmt.Sprintf(\"a configuração %s do Git impede que a busca do último commit, num histórico de %d commits, leia os filtros de caminhos alterados\", graph.readsDisabledBy, graph.commits)), text(\"unset that setting (git config --unset), then run 'git commit-graph write --reachable --changed-paths'\", \"remova essa configuração (git config --unset) e rode 'git commit-graph write --reachable --changed-paths'\"))\n+\tcase graph.filtersUsed:\n+\t\tadd(\"git.commit-graph\", \"ok\", text(\"Git answers last-commit lookups from changed-path filters\", \"o Git responde a busca do último commit pelos filtros de caminhos alterados\"), \"\")\n+\tdefault:\n+\t\tadd(\"git.commit-graph\", \"next\", text(fmt.Sprintf(\"history of %d commits is walked whole by each last-commit lookup: Git has no commit-graph with changed-path filters\", graph.commits), fmt.Sprintf(\"histórico de %d commits percorrido inteiro a cada busca do último commit: o Git não tem commit-graph com filtros de caminhos alterados\", graph.commits)), text(\"run 'git commit-graph write --reachable --changed-paths' (or 'pose doctor --fix --yes')\", \"rode 'git commit-graph write --reachable --changed-paths' (ou 'pose doctor --fix --yes')\"))\n+\t}\n+\n \t// 8. Delivery-integrity / artifact-contract policy roots (issue #17): a\n \t// v1.2.0 `pose install`/`pose update --force` could seed\n \t// .pose/policy/{delivery,artifacts}.json with roots copied verbatim from\nartifact.spec=pose-doctor-recommends-the-commit-graph\nartifact.change_set=cs-9d112d51bccf\nartifact.change_set.base=2bf2adf147bda0b7d8396e025d8f543d08ed2747\nartifact.change_set.head=8cb269059310020b7e6c2605398238546c07b884\nartifact.change_set.commits=33\nartifact.diff_digest=sha256:633e8055ac69401e54fcad8877cb936c9401440365e6ca94b22b69a52cb0fb12\nartifact.claims=5\nartifact.observed=56\nartifact.findings=974\n[!] warning orphan pose-mcp/internal/cli/update_reports_delivered_state_test.go\n    governed tracked path has no spec provenance claim\n    fix: backfill an explicit claim or add an exact reviewed exclusion\n[!] warning orphan pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_routing_test.go\n    governed tracked path has no spec provenance claim\n    fix: backfill an explicit claim or add an exact reviewed exclusion\n[!] warning orphan pose-mcp/internal/cli/state_hooks_test.go\n    governed tracked path has no spec provenance claim\n    fix: backfill an explicit claim or add an exact reviewed exclusion\n[!] warning orphan .github/workflows/security.yml\n    governed tracked path has no spec provenance claim\n    fix: backfill an explicit claim or add an exact reviewed exclusion\n[!] warning orphan pose-mcp/internal/mcpserver/obligations_test.go\n    governed tracked path has no spec provenance claim\n    fix: backfill an explicit claim or add an exact reviewed exclusion\n[!] warning orphan pose-mcp/internal/pose/cache_accounting_test.go\n    governed tracked path has no spec provenance claim\n    fix: backfill an explicit claim or add an exact reviewed exclusion\n[!] warning orphan pose-mcp/internal/pose/action_lifecycle.go\n    governed tracked path has no spec proven