{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport gzip\ns=gzip.open('/usr/share/man/man1/git-config.1.gz','rt').read();i=s.find('commitGraph\\\\\\\\&.maxNewFilters'); print(s[i:i+700])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"commitGraph\\&.maxNewFilters\n.RS 4\nSpecifies the default value for the\n\\fB\\-\\-max\\-new\\-filters\\fR\noption of\n\\fBgit\\fR\n\\fBcommit\\-graph\\fR\n\\fBwrite\\fR\n(c\\&.f\\&.,\n\\fBgit-commit-graph\\fR(1))\\&.\n.RE\n.PP\ncommitGraph\\&.changedPaths\n.RS 4\nIf true, then\n\\fBgit\\fR\n\\fBcommit\\-graph\\fR\n\\fBwrite\\fR\nwill compute and write changed\\-path Bloom filters by default, equivalent to passing\n\\fB\\-\\-changed\\-paths\\fR\\&. If false or unset, changed\\-paths Bloom filters will be written during\n\\fBgit\\fR\n\\fBcommit\\-graph\\fR\n\\fBwrite\\fR\nonly if the filters already exist in the current commit\\-graph file\\&. This matches the default behavior of\n\\fBgit\\fR\n\\fBcommit\\-graph\\fR\n\\fBwrite\\fR\nwithout any\n\\fB\\-\\-\\fR[\\fBno\\-\\fR]\\f\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
